2026-08-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-1144) 'Loop 2 runs first, and its measurements become the numbers the plan checks against.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-1144) 'A filename that matches no key is skipped without a word, so a run reports success and edits nothing.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-1144) 'Check each quantity in `fourloops-plan.usda` against the measurements below.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-1144) 'The image-to-OmniGen2 loop
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-1144) 'Loop 2 exercises OmniGen2 and EditScore with nothing else in the way, so its numbers are the ones the plan layers check their quantities against. Both `fourloops-plan.usda` and `fourloops-etnf.usda` name this file as a source.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-1144) 'Measured on the desk described in `logbook-fourloops-first-runs.md`, which holds the apparatus and the runs these are lifted from.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-1144) 'Run loop 2 first among the four, and let it carry the measurements.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-1144) '**The hazard is a silent skip.** The edit instruction comes from a text input rather than from the filename. A filename that matches no key is skipped without a word, which produces a run that reports success and edits nothing.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-1144) '`DETAILS.md` holds what the first runs measured: what OmniGen2 costs at bf16 and at four bits, what EditScore costs, and what EditScore returns for an instruction the edit actually matched. `fourloops-plan.usda` and `fourloops-etnf.usda` both name that file as a source, so a quantity in either layer is checked against a measurement rather than against a recollection.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-1144) 'RFD66606-1143, RFD66606-1145 and RFD66606-1146 are the other three loops. RFD66606-1128 records four-bit tolerance for another model on the same card.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-1144) 'OmniGen2, and what four bits buys
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-1144) 'Same input, same seed, 1024 square, 30 steps:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-1144) '| precision | weights   | peak      | seconds |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-1144) '| --------- | --------- | --------- | ------: |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-1144) '| bf16      | 14.75 GiB | 17.14 GiB |     131 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-1144) '| NF4       | 4.33 GiB  | 6.72 GiB  |     133 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-1144) 'Four bits bought memory and cost two seconds. Weights fall to 0.29 of bf16 and peak to 0.39, while the wall time moves from 131 to 133 seconds, which is inside the run-to-run spread and should be read as unchanged rather than as slower.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-1144) 'That matters for a 24 GiB desk. At bf16 the peak of 17.14 GiB leaves 6.86 GiB for everything else in the process; at NF4 the peak of 6.72 GiB leaves 17.28. Loop 2 fits either way and loop 4 does not, which is why the plan carries both rows rather than only the one it runs.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-1144) 'CLAUDE.md's generated-synthetic condition 5 decides what may be done with the NF4 row: quantised weights produce no corpus data. So the four-bit form is a way to fit the loop on this desk, and never a way to make data with it. RFD66606-1128 reaches the same place for a different model, and records that four bits bought no speed there either.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-1144) 'Why loop 2 carries the numbers
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-1144) 'Being smallest makes it the one that measures the two components every other loop also uses, so its numbers are the plan's numbers.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-1144) 'What EditScore costs and returns
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-1144) 'RFD66606-1147 holds it. Every loop scores with EditScore and only loops 2 and 3 propose with OmniGen2, so the scorer's figures belong to the plan rather than to this loop. `editscoreMatchingOverall`, `editscoreNonsenseOverall`, `editscorePeakGib512` and `editscorePeakGib1024` all resolve there.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-1144) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-1144) 'Loop 2 is the smallest complete loop: OmniGen2 proposes an edited png, EditScore scores it, OmniGen2 repairs. One propose stage, one scorer, one repair arm, size M, and it runs second because the harness is the only thing it waits on.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1144  1 LINE
 Text:Written
